{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792945819,"nonce":"3SKD6OKZ9fH7OHlD3rkmFEcA8H8=","title":"Programs and terminal in a session: PTY stream and process containers","message":"The session runs programs as pipes today. The terminal needs a PTY (portable-pty, which RayDE's cterm already uses locally) streamed over the session, resize included. In the published form a Durable Object cannot spawn processes, so build and run need a container per session (Cloudflare Containers) with the workspace mounted from the object; decide the mount (the object serves files over the same protocol, or a sync to the container) and the isolation limits for untrusted code.\n\nPart of the browser epic: git-bug ae3a156433377383faa317d5da1f34e6eab10f9a6e0d0ab0456fc0e0277a8382","files":null}]}